  "title": "# Build: claude-badge-vps Brett (voice): \"I need a setting in the Claude badge plugin that has a VP…",
  "asked": "# Build: claude-badge-vps Brett (voice): \"I need a setting in the Claude badge plugin that has a VPS connection and a console connection, and I need to be able to put them on icons only and select which icons for each one.\" Claude badge plugin (apps/console-web/plugins/claude-badge): 1. Two connections, each its own badge/indicator on the banner: - Console connection: the existing test (console AI via axf.llm@1). - VPS connection: the Claude Code login on the VPS (which account, logged in or not, limit hit). Read it with plain code, zero tokens (e.g. the ai-keys/claude-accounts VPS status or a cheap read of /root/.claude.json email + credentials expiry); green = logged in and working, amber = limit hit / out of credits, gray/red = not logged in. 2. Settings (Settings > Plugins > Claude badge): show/hide each one; Icons only switch per badge; pick the icon for each badge and each state (ok / no credit / error), extending the existing Badge icons picker. 3. Covers step 18 of pending item token-usage-log-accounts-plan-studio-control (clock badge watches VPS login): note it there, don't build it twice. 4. Tests, README, screenshots to UI Review, PR to the merge queue. Do NOT land directly. Nothing gets removed. One session for the whole build, read only files you need, no full CLAUDE.md chain. Stay out of notes/tasks/todo and AmberX notification code (other builds). Watch live: Brett can watch the screen you are changing hot-render in the console. Whenever you start work on a screen or element, run `node framework/cli/axf.mjs focus <app> [route] [css-selector] --note \"<what you are changing>\"` (apps: console-web, axhub-web, amberx-droid, walkthrough-studio, demo, framework, console, axhub-android, voicevault). Agent cap: heavy steps (pnpm/npm/vite builds, docker node:22 test runs, Playwright) share a VPS-wide lock. Run each one as `node /opt/axf/deploy/../framework/cli/agent-slots.mjs heavy -- <command>` so only a few run at once. Model switches: a downgrade (e.g. Fable → Opus) is fine. Fable upgrades need no approval right now (Brett, Nov 4 2026: \"If it needs Fable, set it to be Fable\"): a step that needs Fable (schemas, asset types, contracts, engines/kernel, cross-app protocols) is set to Fable and runs on Fable; the switch is recorded on the build. Never launch a step on a higher model than it is pinned to: raise the step first.",
